# STRICT RULE: Next.js Image Optimization

**Every image on the public website MUST use the `<Image>` component from `next/image`. Plain `<img>` tags are FORBIDDEN.**

Violating this rule is an **automatic implementation failure**.

## Required Patterns

### 1. Always Use next/image

```tsx
// ❌ FORBIDDEN - Plain img tag
<img src="/photo.jpg" alt="Photo" />

// ✅ REQUIRED - next/image component
import Image from 'next/image'

<Image 
  src="/photo.jpg" 
  alt="Photo" 
  width={800} 
  height={600} 
/>
```

### 2. Always Define Dimensions or Use Fill

```tsx
// ❌ BAD - No dimensions
<Image src="/photo.jpg" alt="Photo" />

// ✅ GOOD - Explicit dimensions
<Image src="/photo.jpg" alt="Photo" width={800} height={600} />

// ✅ GOOD - Fill with sized container
<div className="relative w-full h-64">
  <Image src="/photo.jpg" alt="Photo" fill className="object-cover" />
</div>
```

### 3. Always Provide Meaningful Alt Text

```tsx
// ❌ BAD - Empty or generic alt
<Image src="/homestay.jpg" alt="" width={400} height={300} />
<Image src="/homestay.jpg" alt="image" width={400} height={300} />

// ✅ GOOD - Descriptive alt
<Image src="/homestay.jpg" alt="Traditional bamboo homestay with mountain view" width={400} height={300} />
```

### 4. Use Priority for Above-the-Fold Images

```tsx
// Hero images - use priority
<Image 
  src="/hero.jpg" 
  alt="Village panorama" 
  width={1920} 
  height={1080} 
  priority 
/>

// Below-the-fold - default lazy loading (do not disable)
<Image src="/gallery-1.jpg" alt="Gallery photo" width={400} height={300} />
```

### 5. Use Sizes for Responsive Images

```tsx
// ❌ BAD - No sizes, mobile downloads desktop-sized files
<Image src="/photo.jpg" alt="Photo" fill />

// ✅ GOOD - Sizes prevent oversized downloads
<Image 
  src="/photo.jpg" 
  alt="Photo" 
  fill 
  sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, (max-width: 1200px) 50vw, 33vw" 
/>
```

### 6. Sanity Images via CDN URL Builder

```tsx
import { urlForImage } from '@/lib/sanity/image'

// ✅ Sanity images through CDN + next/image
<Image
  src={urlForImage(article.coverImage).width(800).height(600).url()}
  alt={article.coverImage.alt || article.title}
  width={800}
  height={600}
/>
```

### 7. Static Images via Static Imports

```tsx
// ✅ Local images - static import for build-time optimization
import homestayPhoto from '@/public/images/homestays/villa-sunrise.jpg'

<Image 
  src={homestayPhoto} 
  alt="Villa Sunrise exterior" 
  placeholder="blur" 
/>
```

## Rationale

The previous website failed because of heavy unoptimized images. Any code that bypasses image optimization is an automatic implementation failure.
